---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { labSamples } from '../../data/labSamples';
import { publicCrates } from '../../data/profile';
---
<Base lang="en" title="Technical lab | Miguel Quevedo" description="Public Rust crates with green GitHub Actions CI and standalone samples in C, Assembly, C++, Swift and PHP.">
  <main id="contenido" class="detail-main wrap">
    <a class="back-link" href="/en/">← Back to portfolio</a>
    <div class="detail-hero lab-hero"><div><p class="section-kicker">INSPECTABLE CODE</p><h1>Technical lab<span>.</span></h1><p class="detail-lede">Standalone open-source repositories with green CI and small engineering samples built to make architecture reviewable.</p></div><div class="detail-badge">GITHUB VERIFIED<br /><strong>3 CI REPOS + 5 SAMPLES</strong></div></div>
    <p class="lab-intro">Every repository and sample listed here is strictly independent of Meson’s private source. All three repositories run strict formatting, static analysis (<code>clippy -D warnings</code> / <code>dart analyze --fatal-infos</code>) and automated tests on Ubuntu &amp; Windows CI.</p>

    <div class="lab-grid">
      {publicCrates.map((crate) => (
        <article>
          <span>{crate.en.eyebrow}</span>
          <h2>{crate.en.title}</h2>
          <p>{crate.en.lead}</p>
          <div class="tags">
            {crate.stack.map((skill) => <span>{skill}</span>)}
          </div>
          <p class="muted" style="font-size:12px;margin-top:10px;">{crate.en.status}</p>
          <div style="display:flex;gap:14px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-top:8px;">
            <a class="text-link" href={crate.repo} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Open GitHub repo ↗</a>
            <a class="text-link" href={crate.ciUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">View Actions CI ↗</a>
          </div>
        </article>
      ))}
    </div>

    <div class="lab-grid" style="margin-top:26px;">
      <article><span>04 / RUST</span><h2>Local synchronization</h2><p>Vector clocks, concurrent changes and pending operations until acknowledgment. Five tests executed.</p><div class="tags"><span>Rust</span><span>Verified</span></div><a class="text-link" href="/en/samples/local-sync/">View sample ↗</a></article>
      {labSamples.map((sample, index) => (
        <article><span>{String(index + 5).padStart(2, '0')} / {sample.en.eyebrow}</span><h2>{sample.en.title}</h2><p>{sample.en.lead}</p><div class="tags">{sample.stack.map((skill) => <span>{skill}</span>)}<span>{sample.verified ? 'Verified' : 'Execution pending'}</span></div><a class="text-link" href={`/en/samples/${sample.slug}/`}>View sample ↗</a></article>
      ))}
    </div>
    <div class="lab-note"><strong>What this proves</strong><p>Alongside Meson architecture previews and live web deployments, these standalone repositories expose inspectable Rust, C99 shared-library FFI, Dart outbox/bindings, x64 Assembly, C++, PHP and Swift implementations with reproducible verification commands.</p></div>
  </main>
</Base>
